{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011689-2e-interesting-paradox-effects","id":1011689,"title":"[2E] Interesting Paradox effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-03T15:15:20-08:00","id":1011689,"title":"[2E] Interesting Paradox effects","content":"I want to make Paradox a bit more nuanced or interesting without changing it's lethality ( at least much ). <b>What would be you cool Paradox effects that are more weird than dangerous to characters? </b>What would be Paradox Reach of those effects?<br /> <br /> Here are my propositions from <b>Life is Strange</b> video game \u2013 Still could not decide on what Paradox Reach should be or radius of the effect. Maybe you will help me?<br /> <br /> <b>Snow in late summer ( area of small town or city district? )</b><br /> <img src=\"https://c7.staticflickr.com/9/8717/16972307182_1bbe9175b5_h.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Mass whales on beach</b><br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-i6N5u2Omdjo/VczurgX1zgI/AAAAAAAAAjE/v_GaDWzAxqo/s1600/Beached%2BWhales.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Sudden eclipse ( area of small town or city district? )</b><br /> <img src=\"http://www.gamecrate.com/sites/default/files/background_image/Life-is-Strange-Episod-II-Out-of-Time-4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Double Moon ( area of small town or city district? ) <img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/1ab9f38b1ad21e8c163c077acaf5613b/tumblr_ofpsk4NG6k1v196kxo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-04-2016, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:49:09-08:00","id":1011738,"title":"","content":"Paradox aren't necessarily lethal in the first place. You don't need to change anything except your ability to interpret and utilize the Paradox rules in an interesting way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T23:41:18-08:00","id":1011881,"title":"","content":"In quest of finding Paradox Reach cost of those is the question here to be asked is those examples should be treated as Abyssal Environmental Tilt? There is nothing dangerous in them ( at least to characters ), they just really weird. I would say less dangerous than proper Environmental Tilt and a bit more disturbing than putting Paradox Condition on subjects only. If first is Reach 3 and second is Reach 1 - then maybe good for those effects would be Reach 2 cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:03:57-08:00","id":1011974,"title":"","content":"The storm as a Abyssal manifestation?<br /> <br /> How about the Deja-Vu from The Matrix. Its easy to double up on descriptions while playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:09:56-08:00","id":1012052,"title":"","content":"<b>Lightning Cage</b><br /> Solid lightning arcs across the area damaging anyone that touches them.<br /> <br /> System: Every time someones moves more than 5 meters, they must roll a reflexive Dexterity+Atheletic with a -2 penalty for every 5 meters beyond the first, Failure means that he suffers damage as if it they was struck by a Major electricity source. If for some reason a character moves twice, say was telekinetically pushed, they are rolled separately(James moves 4 meters, and then was pushed 5 meters in the same turn, he simply rolls once)<br /> <br /> <b>Cruel Wound Revelation</b><br /> A Mages soul forever desire the Truth but to get there, they must cross the Abyss. Damaging the somepart of themselves in the process. This time that's a bit literal, if sligthly reversed<br /> <br /> System: Whenever a Mage has taken damage in the scene they may reflexively roll Gnosis+Stamina each success allows them to ask a question from the Know Nature and Supernal Vision spells on one person in sensory range, this can be anyone not just an attacker. For every question asked he turns one wound into a resistant wound starting from the left of the damage track. A Mage cannot use this effect if they take damage from scouring or when they no longer suffer from a non-resistant wound.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue-as-Sin, Sin-as-Virtue</b><br /> In the land of the Prince of 100.000 Leaves, Virtue is measured by the misery that it brings to others and Vice is the measure of one's own pain.<br /> <br /> System: Anyone in the affected area who fulfills a Virtue causes everyone else to suffer 1 lethal damage and lose 1 willpower, fulfilling a Vice causes restores 1 willpower per wound penalty if they does not suffer any wound penalty they cannot fulfill their Vice. All other restriction on fulfilling a Vice or Virtue still applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:12:47-08:00","id":1012093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011689-2e-interesting-paradox-effects?p=1011974#post1011974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the Deja-Vu from The Matrix. Its easy to double up on descriptions while playing.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu</i> could make nice and elegant Paradox Condition. Maybe like this:<br /> <br /> <b>D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu</b><br /> Character is under constant feeling that she lived through the unfolding events and undermines the reality of this world, seeing all of this as great Lie or some kind of joke. Character get\u2019s -2 penalty to all his actions from this nagging feeling, even if her rational mind try to asses that things like that are not possible.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Time or Mind Ruling magic is cast on character, forcing her to stabilize her perceived events timeline. Or Condition have lapsed, based on spellcaster Wisdom.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You back down from some action or decision due to this Condition or felt \u2018falsehood\u2019 of events. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:07:14-08:00","id":1012160,"title":"","content":"<b>Ferrous Snowfall - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> The snow falling takes on a pinkish hue and smells and feels like some combination of iron and rust. Level 2 Extreme Environment. If a player attempts to open his or her eyes without protective eyewear or other covering they suffer 1 bashing damage and the blinded tilt for the duration of the scene. Players may roll Resolve+Stamina to open their eyes for a turn but will suffer the 1 bashing damage each time they do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Blasphemed Ground - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> Something about this place just feels <i>wrong</i>. In reality the local area has become antithetical to Truth. Everyone in the area is affected by the Distrustful condition.<br /> <br /> Distrustful: the character is prone to disbelieving just about anything, even his closest friends. All attempts to communicate information with him require in a Wits+Persuasion roll contested by the character's Composure+Resolve.<br /> Resolution: the character fails his wits+composure roll five times, or is otherwise unmistakably convinced he is being delusional.<br /> Beat: The character acts against his own interests because he is convinced a friend is lying to him<br /> <br /> <b>Hungry Flames - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> Flames in the area cannot be extinguished by conventional means. Their size cannot be reduced by one per turn using a hose or fire extinguisher. Instead, situations that would normally completely extinguish a fire (oxygen being removed or being submersed in water) will reduce the size of the flame by one per turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Rod - Paradox Condition</b><br /> <br /> Character is affected by the Lightning Rod tilt/condition:<br /> <br /> Lightning Rod (Tilt): The ST rolls a chance die in secret once per turn. Once the successes on the chance die exceed ten, the character is struck by the nearest electricity source.<br /> Lightning Rod (Condition): The ST rolls a chance die once per scene. If the roll succeeds, the character is struck by an electricity source, at the ST's discretion.<br /> Resolution: the character accumulates ten bashing damage worth of electrical damage or the duration of the condition expires<br /> <br /> Condition best applied to Forces-wielding mages in a thunderstorm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Tu quoque - Paradox Condition</b><br /> <br /> The character suffers from a one-directional Shared Fate with the person physically closest to them. This effect functions as the Fate 3 spell Shared Fate with the +1 Reach, except that the mage receives the shared fate of whomever is closest to them.<br /> Resolution: The link is broken by magical means or the duration expires<br /> Beat: The character harms this person (and therefore himself)<br /> <br /> <b>Memory hole - Paradox Condition</b><br /> <br /> The mage suffers from the Amnesia condition but only pertaining to events that happened during this scene.<br /> Resolution: The memories are restored by magical means or the duration expires. This may constitute a breaking point.<br /> Beat: Something problematic arises due to the lost memories","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-05-2016, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T16:37:05-08:00","id":1012253,"title":"","content":"<b>Unhinged Fortune - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> All failures in the area become dramatic failures.<br /> <br /> <b>A Curious Gathering - Spell Gone Awry or Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> The amount of creatures in the area spikes by an order of magnitude. There are suddenly ten times as many birds, rodents, insects, or other wildlife in the area than there were previously. Their attention is fixated on the mage. They don't behave unnaturally, but they could easily be provoked...<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Caucus - Spell Gone Awry or Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> As with the above, only instead of creatures, spirits of lesser and medium rank gather around in increasing numbers.<br /> <br /> <b>Water Water Everywhere - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> Water in the area becomes nonpotable, it evaporates instantly when it comes into contact with human flesh. This causes 1 bashing damage per turn of contact. Water also gains superfluid properties: creeping up surfaces in seeming defiance of gravity.<br /> <br /> <b>Skipping clock - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> Time skips in the area for seconds at a time at random intervals. All recollection of the intervening seconds are lost. This effect makes extended actions all-but impossible. All bonuses to initiative are void.<br /> <br /> <b>Pallor mortis - Paradox Condition</b><br /> <br /> The mage is affected by the condition Corpselike for the duration of the paradox.<br /> <br /> Corpselike: All social rolls suffer a -2 modifier, and all Impressions suffer by one level.<br /> Resolution: The spell is reversed by magical means or the paradox condition expires<br /> Beat: The condition significantly hinders the character from achieving some goal<br /> <br /> <b>Algor Mortis - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b><br /> <br /> Heat does last long in this area. Heat sources seem to provide no real warmth or comfort. Inflicts a level 1 extreme environment. If relevant may also inflict the Icy tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Twisted path - Paradox Condition</b><br /> <br /> The mage suffers from the Twisted Paths condition<br /> <br /> Twisted Paths: Per the spell Lying Maps, the mage is convinced the correct route to his objective is in some wrong, random direction. Attempts to navigate to the correct location, even with GPS, are reduced to a chance die.<br /> Resolution: The mage successfully arrives at the intended location","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-05-2016, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T00:15:04-08:00","id":1012427,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12157\" data-vbnamecard=\"12157\">Kvark</a>, great ideas. But what are simple Conditions on spells subject, what are just light 'weird effects' and what are truly Abyssal Environment Tilt? In other words - What of them should cost Paradox Reach 1, 2 or 3 from above ideas lists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T04:17:27-08:00","id":1012489,"title":"","content":"Went ahead and labeled them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}